# QA Subagent Orchestration

Use project agents under `.cursor/agents/`:

| Agent | Role | Unity mutation |
|-------|------|----------------|
| `qa-coordinator` | Plan, delegate, aggregate | No |
| `qa-inventory` | Map items → scenes/adapters/tests | No (read-only) |
| `qa-scenario-author` | Author/review scenario JSON | No |
| `qa-playtester` | Execute scenarios via QA gateway | **Yes — sole writer** |
| `qa-evidence-reviewer` | Verify artifacts / reject weak PASS | No (read-only) |

## Exclusive lease

- Only **one** `qa-playtester` job may mutate the Unity Editor or active QA session at a time.
- Reject a second concurrent lease owner; do not “share” the Editor across agents.
- Read-only agents may run in parallel (inventory, scenario review, evidence review).

## Handoff contract

Subagents exchange bounded JSON packets including at least:

- `taskId`
- `scenarioIds`
- `evidenceRoot` (under `docs/qa/runs/`)
- `status`: `ready` | `running` | `pass` | `fail` | `blocked`
- `findings`

## Hard constraints

- QA runs use an isolated QA profile; never mutate the normal player save.
- No bug fixes during a QA run; diagnosis/implementation is a separate task.
- Gameplay PASS requires reproduction path, assertions, screenshots, and no new relevant Console exception.
- Never infer PASS from empty Console alone.
- Do not write QA results to Google Sheets as part of this workflow.

## Fallback

If Cursor Task custom-agent delegation is unavailable, run the same role prompts sequentially (e.g. `scripts/qa/run-cursor-qa.ps1` / `cursor-agent -p --output-format json`) while preserving the JSON envelope and single-writer rule.
